        {
          "english": "The 7 Rendille (Rāndili) Names for the Days of the Week & Sabbath/Travel Prohibitions (Hobley 1910, pp. 162–163)",
          "translation": "1st day: Hahat (fast day — no animals prepared for food; prayer to God) • 2nd day: Hura hakhan (Rendille Sabbath — no work done, though animals may be prepared; hura = sun) • 3rd day: Sere (sere = day) • 4th day: Kumat • 5th day: Ser hakhan (prohibited day — may not travel, move grazing ground, or make cattle medicine) • 6th day: Sere adi ('the day of the goats and sheep') • 7th day: Sere gal ('day of the camel')",
          "pronunciation": "ha-hat, hu-ra ha-khan, se-re, ku-mat, ser ha-khan, se-re a-di, se-re gal",
          "context": "C. W. Hobley (1910) 'Ethnology of A-Kamba and Other East African Tribes', Part II, Ch. VI, pp. 162–163",
          "audioFile": null
        }
